--- a/ComicRack/Output/Changes.txt
+++ b/ComicRack/Output/Changes.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-﻿orbitdesign Build 1.71 (based on Community Edition 0.9.184):
+﻿orbitdesign Build 1.72 (based on Community Edition 0.9.184):
 
 * 1.1 FIX: Hardware acceleration stability. Fixed OpenGL extension detection, replaced the deprecated automatic mip map generation that crashed some drivers, checked texture uploads for errors, and added a startup guard that switches hardware acceleration off for one session if ComicRack failed to start last time.
 * 1.2 NEW: Direct2D renderer for the reader. Used by default when hardware acceleration is on, with OpenGL and then software rendering as fallbacks. Handles graphics device resets, uses high quality cubic sampling for "Enable Hardware Filters", and supports paper textures. Start with -hwgl to use the old OpenGL renderer.
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@
 * 1.69 CHANGE: The Glass magnifier now uses the engraved magnifying glass artwork: the zoomed view sits inside its ring, with the handle hanging off to the lower right. The lens is still the 15% larger round view (the artwork scales to fit it). The Simple style keeps its plain round rim, and renderers without hardware acceleration keep the rectangular frame.
 * 1.70 CHANGE: Updated the magnifier artwork and gave it a soft drop shadow, cast down and to the right, outside the lens.
 * 1.71 CHANGE: The Recent Books list in the File menu now keeps the last 30 books (was 20). Also made picking a book from that list always open the book you clicked, even if some of the books above it have since been deleted or moved.
+* 1.72 NEW: Translate Pages (E, or View / right-click menu > Translate Pages). With the separate ComicTranslator helper running, pages are sent to it and come back with the speech bubbles cleaned and the translation lettered in, replacing the page on screen. The page on screen goes first and the next three pages follow, so turning the page usually finds the translation ready. Reading and translating can use a local Ollama model (any language, including vertical Japanese) or Google Translate, chosen on the helper's settings page (View > Translation Settings...). Translated pages are cached, so a book reads instantly the second time.
 
 
 Community Edition Build 0.9.184:
